# Cryptic Coat (CR 701.58a, 701.3b, 702.26): entering, it cloaks the top card of its controller's library - Snapcaster Mage,
# a face-down 2/2 - and attaches itself to it, so the cloaked creature is 3/2 and can't be blocked. A creature card cloaked
# may be turned face up any time its controller has priority by paying its mana cost (CR 701.58a, 708.8): {1}{U}, a special
# action. Turned face up it is the same permanent, now a 2/1 Snapcaster Mage with flash, still equipped: 3/1.
#
# Black Lotus pays the Coat; Sol Ring (cast with the Island) and Mox Sapphire pay the {1}{U} to turn the Mage face up.

